#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:378
#, no-c-format
msgid "Who made this game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The kdegames team. You can find their website <ulink url=\"http://games.kde."
"org\">here</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where can I get cheatcodes?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "You cannot get cheatcodes for &kde; games."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I know what does the molecule looks like?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can view the molecule on the reference screen located in the top right "
"corner of the game screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where is the reference screen?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The reference screen is located in the top right corner of the game screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I move a game piece (atom)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a game piece (atom) use your mouse cursor to click on it. At this "
"time the available directional icon will become visible. Click on the "
"corresponding directional icon to make a game piece move into the desired "
"direction. Alternatively, you can use your keyboard to move the pieces. Use "
"the &Tab; key to switch between the items, and the cursor keys to move them "
"once selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I use the keyboard to control the pieces (atoms)?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:399
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. Use &Tab; key to switch between the items, and he cursor keys to move "
"them once selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I move a piece (atom) it goes right past the place where I want it. How "
"do I make it stop there?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You don't. Once an atom begins moving, it will not stop until it meets "
"either a wall or another piece."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "I have stuck. How can I restart the game?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To restart &katomic; choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Game</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Restart</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. "
"Alternatively you can press <keycap>F5</keycap> key on your keyboard to "
"restart the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "I cannot beat the level. Is there a hint system, or a solver?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No. Unfortunately at this time &katomic; does not feature a hint system. So "
"the only way to finish a level is to solve it on your own."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:414
#, no-c-format
msgid "I did something wrong. Can I undo?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. To undo a wrong move select <menuchoice><guimenu>Move</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. "
"Alternatively you can press <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</"
"keycap></keycombo> on your keyboard."
msgstr ""

